# Tanner's private working docs — local only, never committed or pushed.
# The "Combined Idea Checklist" is a personal scratchpad; keep it off GitHub.
# (Leading * matches the "(C) SpaceSuck — " prefix without depending on the
#  em-dash byte, so the rule holds even if the prefix changes.)
*Combined Idea Checklist.md

# Pre-rebuild asset backups. A rebuild writes these beside the asset; their
# content is always already in git history, so they're scratch — never commit
# them. (Recover one with: git show <commit>^:planets/earth.glb > earth.glb)
*.bak

# Blender/Python bytecode from the build scripts
__pycache__/

# Local convenience symlink into the Blender masters volume. It is an ABSOLUTE
# path to one machine's disk, so committing it hands every clone a dangling
# link — and it leaked into v79.1 via `git add -A`. The symlink itself stays on
# disk; git just stops tracking it.
masters

# The world inspector. It's a WORKBENCH, not part of the game — it exists to
# look hard at a planet BEFORE that planet is fit to ship. This repo is public
# and Pages serves the whole root, so tracking it published a private tool at a
# guessable URL. Same slip as the symlink above. The file stays on disk and is
# used the same way (./play.sh, then localhost:8123/planet-lab.html); git just
# never carries it again.
planet-lab.html
